<title>USA: U.S. Jan industrial output unchanged from Dec.</title>
<headline>U.S. Jan industrial output unchanged from Dec.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Board report of U.S. industrial production and capacity utilization, seasonally adjusted.</p>
<p> Total Industrial:	  Jan    Dec    Nov    Oct   Jan97/96</p>
<p> Production, Pct Change   UNCH   0.5    0.8    0.2    4.7</p>
<p> Previous Estimates		  0.7    0.8   UNCH</p>
<p> Production Index-X	 000.0  129.1  128.1  127.1</p>
<p> -				Jan    Dec    Nov    Oct   Jan96</p>
<p> Pct of Capacity Use     83.3   83.5    83.4  83.0   82.4</p>
<p> Previous Estimates		 83.5    83.2  82.8</p>
<p>X--1987 equals 100.</p>
<p>Industrial Production,Seasonally adjusted percent changes:</p>
<p> -				Jan    Dec    Nov    Oct  Jan97/96</p>
<p> Major Market Products    0.1    0.2    1.0    0.1    4.8</p>
<p> -Consumer Goods	    UNCH   0.7    1.1    0.3    4.2</p>
<p> -Business Equipment	0.8    0.4    0.9    0.4    7.8</p>
<p> -Construc.Supplies	-0.7   -1.8    1.6   -1.8    5.2</p>
<p> Major Materials	   -0.1    0.8    0.4    0.4    4.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing Industry  -0.2    0.7    0.8    0.2    5.1</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	     UNCH   0.6    1.0   -0.1    6.3</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	  -0.7    0.9   -3.8    2.2    5.2</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks     2.4    0.1    7.1   -7.9    8.8</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	-0.4    0.9    0.5    0.5    3.7</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products    -1.4    0.2   -0.9    1.4    0.9</p>
<p> Mining Industry	   -0.7    1.4    UNCH   UNCH   5.3</p>
<p> Utilities Industry	 2.9   -2.9    1.1    0.7    0.4</p>
<p>Percent of Capacity: Manufacturing, Mining, Utilities:</p>
<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Jan    Dec    Nov    Oct   Jan'96</p>
<p> Manufacturing	     82.2   82.7   82.4   82.0   81.5</p>
<p>Percent of Capacity: Manufacturing, Mining, Utilities:</p>
<p>    (Seasonally Adj.)     Jan    Dec    Nov    Oct   Jan'96</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	    81.5   81.9   81.8   81.5   81.4</p>
<p> --Primary Metals	  89.2   90.2   89.6   93.5   87.8</p>
<p> --Autos/Light Trucks    79.6   77.8   77.8   72.8   74.1</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods	83.1   83.6   83.0   82.7   81.6</p>
<p> --Petroleum Products    93.2   94.5   94.4   95.3   92.8</p>
<p> Mining			91.6   92.3   91.0   91.0   86.9</p>
<p> Utilities		   89.4   87.1   89.9   89.0   91.0</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected January industrial production to rise 0.1 percent and estimated that January capacity use would be at a rate of 83.4 percent.</p>
<p>The Fed said that production of business equipment rose again in January but consumer goods were flat and output of construction supplies fell for a second straight month.</p>
<p>Motor vehicle assemblies rose in January to a rate of 6 million a year for cars from 5.8 million in December. For light trucks the assembly rate was up to 6.1 million from 6.0 million.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles and parts, January industrial output fell 0.1 percent after rising a revised 0.5 percent in December instead of 0.8 percent as the Fed previously reported.</p>
